            <div xml:id="d575">

                <pb facs="0882" n="746" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg746"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3299: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Culbertson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-03-16T10:00:00-04:00">March 16, 1929—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>41. With reference to paragraph 4 in your 29, March 15, 3 p.m., remind Cady that
                    all the ports of Peru and Chile north of Valparaiso including the present Arica
                    any [<hi rendition="#italic">are</hi>?] lighterage ports. I have assumed that
                    the port either at San José or Escritos would be of the same character.</p>
                <p>Copy furnished Lima.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
